    {"name": "CRQC", "type": "quantum", "notes": "Cryptographically relevant quantum computer: enough logical qubits + error correction to run Shor against RSA-2048/ECC at operational cost. No public evidence one exists today. Resource estimates have compressed (20M -> <1M -> possibly ~100k physical, contested).", "capability_tier": "unknown", "source": ["https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/post-quantum-cryptography"]},
    {"name": "HNDL", "type": "capability", "notes": "Harvest-Now-Decrypt-Later. NSA 2021 public warning: collect ciphertext now, decrypt after Q-Day. Damage to long-lived secrets is already incurred; only the decryption is deferred.", "capability_tier": "industrial", "source": ["https://media.defense.gov/2021/Aug/04/2002821837/-1/-1/0/CSI_CNSA_2.0_FAQ_.PDF"]},
    {"name": "TNFL", "type": "capability", "notes": "Trust-Now-Forge-Later (integrity twin of HNDL). After Shor, public keys yield private keys: old signatures, certs, ePassport Passive Authentication become forgeable. HNDL breaks secrecy; TNFL breaks authentication.", "capability_tier": "industrial", "source": ["https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/post-quantum-cryptography"]},
    {"name": "Silent_QDay", "type": "capability", "notes": "Strategic reading (graded): first CRQC owner has a concealment incentive. Public 2030/2035 deadlines assume an observable Q-Day. Not a claim that any actor has a CRQC.", "capability_tier": "unknown", "source": ["https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/post-quantum-cryptography"]},
